{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>That I lift up his face</b> — HaShem lifts up the face of the righteous in this world, but in the world to come it is not so. Far be it that HaShem do a vile thing. Rather, because Job's companions justified HaShem, if HaShem bring evil upon them they would say, 'They that wander in spirit' — lo, this is a vile thing. The words of Job and his companions I shall yet explain, and in what they erred. And HaShem said: let them go to Job, because they condemned him without cause, and behold it has become clear that Job was a complete righteous man."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "The clause 'יאמרו תועי רוח הנה זה דבר נבלה' is rendered hyper-literally; the syntactic relationship between the three phrases is obscure in the original and may reflect a compressed or elliptical argument left intentionally unresolved."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:47.473370983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}